---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
import { profile, projects, categories, categoryUrl, projectUrl } from '../data/portfolio';
import '../styles/home.css';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const findProject = (slug: string) => projects.find(project => project.slug === slug)!;
const atlas = findProject('gpu-signal-atlas');
const signalstory = findProject('signalstory');
const hatti = findProject('hatti-quest');
const moreWork = [
  { project: findProject('incidentlens'), note: 'Following the evidence through an incident.' },
  { project: findProject('llm-serving-observatory'), note: 'A closer look at what happens behind a prompt.' },
  { project: findProject('racetime-copilot'), note: 'Catching up on a race, without losing the story.' },
];
---
<Base pageClass="homepage" themeColor="#f4efe5" title="Siva Babu — A personal workbench" description="Hi, I’m Siva. I build to figure things out: systems, observability, race stories, and language adventures. Come look around my personal workbench.">
  <section class="personal-hero container" aria-labelledby="hello-title">
    <div class="personal-intro">
      <p class="hello">Hi, I’m Siva.<span class="hello-wave" aria-hidden="true">✳</span></p>
      <h1 id="hello-title">I build to<br/>figure things <em>out.<svg viewBox="0 0 190 17" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 11C48 2 115 4 181 7M8 15C67 9 129 8 187 10"/></svg></em></h1>
      <p class="personal-lede">Mostly systems and observability. Sometimes race videos, language adventures, and whatever question leads to the next experiment.</p>
      <div class="personal-actions"><a class="ink-link" href="#selected-work">Have a look around <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a href={base+'projects/'} class="quiet-link">All {projects.length} projects <Arrow size={16}/></a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="portrait-composition">
      <span class="portrait-orbit" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <p class="margin-note portrait-note">a face behind<br/>the repositories<svg viewBox="0 0 90 75" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 4C2 36 34 51 79 61M65 48L80 61L62 68"/></svg></p>
      <figure class="portrait-paper"><div class="portrait-photo"><img src={base+'images/siva-babu.png'} width="460" height="460" alt="Siva Babu" fetchpriority="high" /></div><figcaption><span>Siva Babu</span><span>From my GitHub profile.</span></figcaption></figure>
      <div class="question-slip"><span class="slip-label">A recurring question</span><p>What would make<br/>this easier to<br/><em>understand?</em></p><svg viewBox="0 0 170 13" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 8C47 1 107 1 166 6"/></svg></div>
      <span class="small-stamp">systems ↔ stories</span>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="chapter-line container"><span>Code, experiments & things worth sharing.</span><a href="#selected-work">A few things I’ve made <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a></div>
  <section class="personal-work container" id="selected-work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
    <div class="work-introduction"><div><p class="page-note">From the workbench</p><h2 id="work-title">Different questions.<br/><em>Same curiosity.</em></h2></div><p>A few projects that show the range.<br/>Start with whichever catches your eye.</p></div>
    <article class="atlas-story">
      <a href={projectUrl(base,atlas.slug)} class="signal-sketch" aria-label="Explore GPU Signal Atlas">
        <div class="sketch-top"><span>GPU Signal Atlas</span><span aria-hidden="true">01 / SYSTEMS</span></div>
        <div class="sketch-question">A number.<br/><em>But what does it mean?</em></div>
        <svg class="signal-line" viewBox="0 0 520 90" aria-hidden="true"><path class="sketch-grid-line" d="M0 70H520M0 35H520M50 0V90M150 0V90M250 0V90M350 0V90M450 0V90"/><path class="sketch-wave" d="M0 69L34 69L42 60L54 73L66 56L79 68L112 67L127 62L142 72L158 65L173 64L191 22L208 70L223 65L244 64L262 42L280 67L302 65L317 12L335 69L352 57L373 65L395 65L414 36L435 67L455 66L473 59L492 69L520 64"/></svg>
        <div class="sketch-steps"><span>signal</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span>context</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span>evidence</span></div>
        <div class="sketch-bottom"><span>A sketch of the idea</span><span class="sketch-open" aria-hidden="true"><Arrow diagonal size={22}/></span></div>
      </a>
      <div class="atlas-copy"><span class="story-number">01</span><p class="story-label">Understanding systems</p><h3>A metric is only<br/><em>the beginning.</em></h3><p>GPU telemetry gives you numbers. GPU Signal Atlas connects those numbers to documentation and cited explanations, so there’s a path from a signal to the evidence behind it.</p><a class="ink-link" href={projectUrl(base,atlas.slug)}>Inside GPU Signal Atlas <Arrow size={18}/></a></div>
    </article>
    <div class="story-pair">
      <article class="learning-story">
        <a class="story-image signalstory-image" href={projectUrl(base,signalstory.slug)} aria-label="Explore SignalStory"><img src={base+'images/'+signalstory.image} width={signalstory.imageWidth} height={signalstory.imageHeight} alt="SignalStory’s four-part observability learning journey" loading="lazy"/><span class="image-corner" aria-hidden="true"><Arrow diagonal size={20}/></span></a>
        <p class="image-caption">SignalStory · a view from the Python studio</p>
        <div class="story-copy"><span class="story-number">02</span><p class="story-label">Learning by doing</p><h3>Make it click.<br/><em>Then make it yours.</em></h3><p>Observability is easier to grasp when you can change something and see what happens. SignalStory follows one checkout story through measurements, queries, traces, and evidence.</p><a class="ink-link" href={projectUrl(base,signalstory.slug)}>Meet SignalStory <Arrow size={18}/></a></div>
        <a class="pencil-link" href={base+'learn/'}>More ways to learn by doing <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="family-story">
        <p class="margin-note family-note">a different kind<br/>of connection</p>
        <a class="story-image hatti-image" href={projectUrl(base,hatti.slug)} aria-label="Explore Hatti Quest"><img src={base+'images/'+hatti.image} width={hatti.imageWidth} height={hatti.imageHeight} alt="Hatti Quest’s language adventure through the hills" loading="lazy"/><span class="image-corner" aria-hidden="true"><Arrow diagonal size={20}/></span></a>
        <p class="image-caption">Hatti Quest · a detail from the adventure</p>
        <div class="story-copy"><span class="story-number">03</span><p class="story-label">Language & family</p><h3>A little adventure.<br/><em>A little closer to home.</em></h3><p>Hatti Quest takes a gentler turn: small Badaga language adventures, familiar words, and family voices. Software that makes room for the things we want to pass on.</p><a class="ink-link" href={projectUrl(base,hatti.slug)}>Step into Hatti Quest <Arrow size={18}/></a></div>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="more-work"><p class="page-note">Also on the workbench</p><div class="work-lines">{moreWork.map(({project,note})=><a href={projectUrl(base,project.slug)}><span class="work-line-title">{project.title}</span><span class="work-line-note">{note}</span><Arrow diagonal size={19}/></a>)}</div></div>
  </section>
  <section class="work-drawers container" aria-labelledby="drawers-title"><div><p class="page-note">Keep looking</p><h2 id="drawers-title">There’s more<br/><em>in the drawers.</em></h2><a class="ink-link" href={base+'projects/'}>The whole collection <Arrow size={18}/></a></div><nav aria-label="Browse projects by category">{categories.map((category,index)=><a href={categoryUrl(base,category.id)}><span class="drawer-index">0{index+1}</span><span>{category.name}</span><span class="drawer-count">{category.count}</span><Arrow size={17}/></a>)}</nav></section>
  <section class="personal-note container" id="about" aria-labelledby="note-title"><div class="note-heading"><span class="note-star" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><p class="page-note">A note from Siva</p></div><div class="note-body"><h2 id="note-title">The common thread?<br/><em>Wanting to understand.</em></h2><p>My projects wander between infrastructure, visual learning, race coverage, and language. What connects them is wanting to understand something well enough to make it useful—and sharing what I build along the way.</p><p>If something here overlaps with a question you’re thinking about, I’d be glad to compare notes.</p><a class="ink-link" href={profile.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Find me on GitHub <Arrow diagonal size={18}/></a><p class="sign-off">Thanks for stopping by.<br/><span>Siva</span></p></div></section>
</Base>
